[{"source": "codebase", "severity": "warning", "category": "memory-safety", "title": "New test_role_absent_demand_inert double-frees the trimmed entries array (allocator flags 'bad free' in catalogs_destroy)", "location": "core/demand_test.odin:526-538", "evidence": "core/demand_test.odin:526 `defer catalogs_destroy(cat2)` ... :529-530 `trimmed := make([dynamic]Demand_Entry, 0, 4, context.allocator)` / `defer delete(trimmed)` ... :537-538 `delete(e3.entries)` / `e3.entries = trimmed`. core/catalog.odin:981-982 `for i in 0..<len(cat.demand.eras) {` / `delete(cat.demand.eras[i].entries)`. Live run of `odin test core -o:speed` at HEAD d0c2c38: `:: core.test_role_absent_demand_inert` ... `+++ bad free        @ 0x448001478 [catalog.odin:982:catalogs_destroy()]` (suite still prints \"Finished 194 tests ... All tests were successful\").", "detail": "e3.entries aliases trimmed's backing, so catalogs_destroy(cat2) frees the same allocation defer delete(trimmed) already freed. Real double-free/UB in the round-3 delta test; passes only because odin test doesn't fail on allocator warnings.", "recommended_fix": "Delete the `defer delete(trimmed)` line — ownership of `trimmed` transfers to cat2.demand.eras[2].entries and catalogs_destroy(cat2) frees it exactly once."}, {"source": "codebase", "severity": "note", "category": "coverage-gap", "title": "Re-pinned W9 fixture makes the 'hosts >= 8' growth pin tautological; its failure message still attributes the crowd to growth", "location": "core/demand_test.odin:726", "evidence": "core/demand_test.odin:615-622 seeds the crowd pre-growth: `host_pos := [8][2]i32{...}` / `for hp in host_pos { topology_spawn_node(&s.topology, host_idx, hp, cat) }` / `camp_pos := [8][2]i32{{6, 20}, ...}` (6 entries) / `for cp in camp_pos { topology_spawn_node(&s.topology, camp_idx, cp, cat) }`. Lines 699-700 count `if s.topology.node_role[ns] == .Content_Host || s.topology.node_role[ns] == .Campus { hosts += 1 }`. Line 726: `testing.expectf(t, hosts >= 8, \"growth must place >= 8 streaming-capable terminals (content_hosts + campuses) by the surge window (got %d) — the aggregation crowd\", hosts)`", "detail": "The fixture pre-seeds 14 streaming-capable terminals and this test never removes nodes, so hosts >= 8 can never fail — the pin no longer bites, and its message misattributes the crowd to growth placement.", "recommended_fix": "Either reword the message to state the crowd is seeded, or count only growth-spawned terminals (spawned after run start) so the growth-placement claim is actually pinned."}]
